==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|deyja}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*dawjaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈteiːja/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eiːja|lang=is}}
*: Homophones: {{l|is|deigja}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|dó|dóu|dáið}}

# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[die]]{{jump|is|die|s}}
#: ''Hún '''dó''' úr krabbameini.''
#:: She '''died''' of cancer.
#: ''Hundruð manna '''dóu''' úr hor.''
#:: Hundreds '''died''' of hunger.
#: ''Við munum öll '''deyja'''!''
#:: We are all going to '''die'''!
#: ''Að '''deyja''' úr kulda.''
#:: To '''die''' from exposure.
# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[pass out]] from drinking
# {{lb|is|intransitive|of fire}} to [[go out]]{{jump|is|of fire, go out|s}}
# {{lb|is|intransitive|nautical|of the ocean}} to [[calm down]], to [[subside]]
# {{lb|is|intransitive|of grass}} to [[wither]]

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s6|d|ey|j=j}}

====Derived terms====
{{der-top}}
* {{l|is|deyja af}}, {{l|is|deyja niður}}, {{l|is|deyja út}} (''of weather or sea'' to calm down)
* {{l|is|deyja burt}} (''archaic'' to die)
* {{l|is|deyja drottni sínum}}
* {{l|is|deyja ekki ráðalaus}} (to not to give up easily)
* {{l|is|deyja fyrir hendi|deyja fyrir hendi einhver}} (to die at the hands of someone)
{{der-mid}}
* {{l|is|deyja niður}} (to die in heaps)
* {{l|is|deyja úr hor}}, {{l|is|deyja úr hungri}} (to starve to death, to die of starvation, to die of hunger)
* {{l|is|deyja út af}} (to die a natural death, ''confer'' [[lognast út af]])
* {{l|is|deyja úti}} (''of hay'' not make it to the barn, left out in times of autumn)
* {{l|is|deyja út}} (to become extinct, to die out)
{{der-bottom}}

